How to start with UI in Figma?
==============================

Getting started with UI design in Figma
=======================================
Step-by-Step Beginner Guide to UI Design in Figma

1. Create a Figma Account
=========================
Go to:
Figma Official Website (figma.com)
You can use it:
In a web browser
On Windows
On macOS

2. Understand the Figma Interface
=================================
Main areas:
===========
Toolbar → shape, frame, text tools
Layers Panel → list of UI elements
Canvas → design workspace
Properties Panel → colors, size, effects

3. Start with a Frame (Screen)
=============================
In Figma, a screen/page is called a Frame.

Shortcut:
Press F

Choose:
Mobile screen
Desktop screen
Tablet screen

Example:
iPhone 15 frame
Desktop 1440px frame

4. Learn Basic UI Elements
===========================
Practice creating:
Buttons
Text fields
Navigation bars
Cards
Icons
Menus
Important Tools
Tool	Shortcut
Frame	F
Rectangle	R
Text	T
Move	V
Pen	P

5. Use Auto Layout
==================
Auto Layout helps elements resize and align automatically.
It is one of the most important Figma features.

Example:
Buttons resize with text
Lists align automatically

6. Learn Basic Design Principles
================================
UI Design Principles
====================
Alignment
Contrast
Consistency
Spacing
Typography
Visual hierarchy

Example:
Larger text = more important
Consistent colors improve usability

7. Use Components
=================
Components are reusable UI elements.

Example:
One button design used everywhere

If you edit the main component:
All copies update automatically

8. Practice with Small Projects
===============================
Start simple:
Login screen
Calculator UI
Music player UI
To-do app
Dashboard UI

9. Use Free UI Kits
===================
UI kits provide ready-made components.

Search inside Figma Community:
Mobile UI Kit
Material Design
iOS UI Kit

10. Learn Prototyping
=====================
Figma can create interactive prototypes.

You can:
Connect screens
Add animations
Simulate app flow

Beginner Learning Path
======================
Week 1
======
Learn tools
Create simple shapes/layouts
Week 2
======
Build small screens
Learn typography/colors
Week 3
======
Learn components and auto layout
Week 4
======
Create full app UI

Recommended Beginner Projects
=============================
Difficulty	          Project
==========            =======
Easy	                Login Page
Easy	                Calculator UI
Medium	              Music App
Medium	              Food Delivery App
Advanced	            Admin Dashboard

Helpful Resources
=================
Figma Learn Center
Figma YouTube Channel

Simple Workflow
===============
Research → Wireframe → UI Design → Prototype → Test

Important Beginner Tip
======================
Do not start by designing complex apps immediately.

First master:
Frames
Auto Layout
Components
Spacing
Typography

These are the foundations of professional UI design.
